          "source": "NCERT Exemplar",
          "question": "$\\displaystyle\\int e^x\\left(\\dfrac{1 - x}{1 + x^2}\\right)^2 dx$ is equal to:",
          "options": [
            "$\\dfrac{e^x}{1 + x^2} + C$",
            "$\\dfrac{-e^x}{1 + x^2} + C$",
            "$\\dfrac{e^x}{\\left(1 + x^2\\right)^2} + C$",
            "$\\dfrac{-e^x}{\\left(1 + x^2\\right)^2} + C$"
          ],
          "solution": {
            "answer": "(A) $\\dfrac{e^x}{1 + x^2} + C$",
            "concept": "$\\displaystyle\\int e^x\\,[f(x) + f'(x)]\\,dx = e^x f(x) + C$",
            "steps": [
              { "do": "Expand $(1 - x)^2 = (1 + x^2) - 2x$", "math": "\\left(\\dfrac{1 - x}{1 + x^2}\\right)^2 = \\dfrac{1}{1 + x^2} - \\dfrac{2x}{\\left(1 + x^2\\right)^2}" },
              { "do": "Take $f(x) = \\dfrac{1}{1 + x^2}$", "math": "f'(x) = -\\dfrac{2x}{\\left(1 + x^2\\right)^2}" },
              { "do": "So the integrand is $e^x[f(x) + f'(x)]$", "math": "\\displaystyle\\int e^x\\left[\\dfrac{1}{1 + x^2} - \\dfrac{2x}{(1 + x^2)^2}\\right]dx = \\dfrac{e^x}{1 + x^2} + C", "marks": 1 }
            ],
            "mistake": "Expanding $(1 - x)^2$ as $1 - x^2$; the middle term $-2x$ is what creates $f'(x)$."
          }
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "marks": 1,
          "type": "mcq",
          "source": "NCERT Exemplar",
          "question": "If $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{x^3}{\\sqrt{1 + x^2}}\\,dx = a\\left(1 + x^2\\right)^{3/2} + b\\sqrt{1 + x^2} + C$, then:",
          "options": [
            "$a = \\dfrac{1}{3},\\; b = 1$",
            "$a = -\\dfrac{1}{3},\\; b = 1$",
